<title>INDONESIA: Astra says Q1 net up to 119.83 bln rph.</title>
<headline>Astra says Q1 net up to 119.83 bln rph.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		     (in billion rupiah unless earnings per share)</p>
<p>    Net profit				   119.83 vs  73.46</p>
<p>    Annualised earnings per share (rph)    412  vs 253</p>
<p>Non-financial services</p>
<p>    Total revenues			  3,120.60  vs  2,885.27</p>
<p>    Gross profit				595.33  vs    539.87</p>
<p>    Operating profit			  284.46  vs    245.83</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			    142.66  vs    101.59</p>
<p>Financial services</p>
<p>    Total revenues			     354.57 vs    298.86</p>
<p>    Total expenses			     294.48 vs    242.93</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit				60.09 vs	55.93</p>
<p>Consolidated results</p>
<p>    Total pre-tax profit		     202.75 vs     157.52</p>
<p>    Retained earnings			1,658.21 vs   1,247.02</p>
<p>NOTE: PT Astra International is one of Indonesia's largest conglomerates, with interests ranging from vehicle assembly and financial services to agribusiness.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
